### Day 10/50 — Relationships in Databases

In a database, not every piece of information exists independently.

Some records are connected to one another.

One student can register for many events.  
One event can have many students.  
And sometimes, one record connects two completely different tables.

That's how relationships work in databases.

There are different types of relationships — 
one-to-one, one-to-many and many-to-many

And honestly, it's interesting how differently things can be connected.

Not everything has to follow the same pattern.

Some connections are between two individuals.  
Some involve many people.  
And some exist only because of a common purpose.

** Maybe that's what makes relationships interesting too - there isn't just one way for two things to be connected **
